From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: shell32: files dropped on a folder are copied or moved into it

The file system folder's drop target was a stub that printed what it
would do. Now a drop of the shell's ID list or of any program's CF_HDROP onto a
folder or a drive copies, moves or links as Windows decides: Ctrl copies,
Shift moves, Ctrl+Shift or Alt makes shortcuts, otherwise a move on the same
volume and a copy to another; never a move into the folder the files are in.
The copy goes through SHFileOperation, so it has the progress window and the
Replace or Skip questions. GetUIObjectOf(IID_IDropTarget) for a folder item
gives that folder's drop target, not its parent's.

Gate: test/explorer2-gate.sh (a file dropped on the navigation pane).
